# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Private while this repo is public.
#
# It is public only because GitHub Pages requires it. Everything below either
# describes the product, targets a commercial site, or maps the live backend's
# attack surface, so none of it goes out until the repo itself is private.
# All of it stays on disk — it is excluded from git, not deleted.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The product brief.
DESCRIPTION.md

# Internal notes: the distribution runbook and the commercial-endpoint probes
# behind the "no paid stats feed" decision.
docs/

# Schema and auth configuration. RLS is the entire security boundary, and
# config.toml records which auth protections are currently off.
supabase/

